90e412d48130bd2a8de435e5af8b3fec077\", \"decision\": \"reject\", \"reason\": \"Under the Relevance and Commercial incentives sections, this is a training-method comparison that primarily cites a 2026 review of vest trials and in-house calculator notes rather than gear testing, with no hands-on gear evidence about performance at Mammoth. It is published by a source with affiliate commissions and GORUCK-supplied review units, and the text itself says it is not a head-to-head gear comparison. Under the Making the decision section, the evidence does not support a gear conclusion, so I reject it rather than defer it.\", \"piece_ids\": []}\n{\"item_id\": \"feed:https://ruckauthority.com/weight-loss/can-rucking-be-your-only-exercise\", \"version_id\": \"2a7879b683f10ab9328299cfac2d2719b7bb49cf69c7d2c7ad301806975cbe97\", \"decision\": \"reject\", \"reason\": \"Under the Relevance section, this is a general fitness and training-program article about whether rucking alone is enough, not gear evaluation for Mammoth conditions. It is also published by a source with affiliate commissions and GORUCK-supplied review units, and it relies on general guidelines and its own program recommendations rather than gear testing. Under Making the decision, it is out of scope.\", \"piece_ids\": []}\n{\"item_id\": \"feed:https://ruckauthority.com/weight-loss/long-term-rucking-for-weight-loss-a-periodization-approach\", \"version_id\": \"7d4232883e8b52f19a788f2a4e07b12ae68877f0d11149a4cc16d2ced85530a8\", \"decision\": \"reject\", \"reason\": \"Under Relevance, this is a weight-loss training plan rather than gear evaluation, and its own text states that no controlled trial has tested a periodized rucking plan for weight loss, so the content rests on the author's coaching recommendations. It is from a source with affiliate commissions and GORUCK-supplied review units, and it has no independent testing of gear. Under Making the decision and Unsupported claims, it is out of scope and rests on unsupported claims.\", \"piece_ids\": []}\n{\"item_id\": \"feed:https://ruckauthority.com/weight-loss/rucking-calorie-calculator-guide\", \"version_id\": \"cdb5d280224dc2d9ebac2dfb3d4d83116e742df6ced2b09fd15d435ed04814c0\", \"decision\": \"reject\", \"reason\": \"Under Relevance, this is a calorie-estimation guide built on the publisher's own calculator and a Pandolf model, not gear evaluation, and it is a promotional tool page with links to other products. Under Credibility and Commercial incentives, the source has affiliate commissions and GORUCK-supplied review units, and the calorie figures are model estimates, not measured performance of any gear. Under Making the decision, it is out of scope.\", \"piece_ids\": []}\n{\"item_id\": \"feed:https://ruckauthority.com/weight-loss/rucking-for-women\", \"version_id\": \"20f721d5647cef2e73060b9f7115ccfde4156b261a5ccc48086e1118abbd3427\", \"decision\": \"reject\", \"reason\": \"Under Relevance, this is a general guide to women's rucking, including fat-loss, bone health, menstrual cycle, and pregnancy guidance, and it does not evaluate gear. Under Commercial incentives, the source has affiliate commissions and GORUCK-supplied review units, and it links to product guides without independent testing of gear. Under Making the decision, it is out of scope, and it includes medical guidance that is not evidence about equipment.\", \"piece_ids\": []}\n{\"item_id\": \"feed:https://ruckauthority.com/weight-loss/rucking-vs-running-weight-loss\", \"version_id\": \"a5e4e0e8c6b9c466bc4d5a2dec752ffc2325b52918c58d0e1e5acd61253e1242\", \"decision\": \"reject\", \"reason\": \"Under Relevance, this compares rucking and running as training activities for cardio and weight loss, and it does not evaluate gear. Under Commercial incentives, the source has affiliate commissions and GORUCK-supplied review units, and its calorie figures are model estimates. Under Making the decision, it is out of scope.\", \"piece_ids\": []}\n{\"item_id\": \"feed:https://ruckauthority.com/gear/goruck-rucker-5-0-review\", \"version_id\": \"66af62696466704fa6aa3667b98d7310f8b80deddad80459b13077cda96833c3\", \"decision\": \"defer\", \"reason\": \"Under Relevance, this is a backpack review in scope, and under Credibility the reviewer carried the pack on a filmed hike with a 20 lb plate, which is firsthand field testing. However, under Commercial incentives, GORUCK supplied the review unit and the source earns affiliate commissions, so the praise carries less weight as independent confirmation. The review presents mostly one reviewer's single outing without independent corroboration or measured data, and its central verdict rests on that single test, so the evidence is too thin to rely on yet under Making the decision.\", \"piece_ids\": []}\n{\"item_id\": \"feed:https://ruckauthority.com/gear/goruck-rucker-5-0-vs-4-0-review\", \"version_id\": \"54479d2596b49a0ecdf91bff88af124cc281bbeee27e613103538767d586a5d2\", \"decision\": \"defer\", \"reason\": \"Under Relevance, this compares two backpacks, which is in scope, but the reviewer has carried only the 5.0 and says the 4.0 comparison comes from GORUCK's published information. Under Commercial incentives, GORUCK supplied the 5.0 for review and the source earns affiliate commissions, and under Credibility, the upgrade claims about the lumbar pad rest on one reviewer's outing without independent measurement. Under Making the decision, the evidence is too thin to rely on yet, and the piece largely repeats the already-deferred 5.0 review, so it is deferred.\", \"piece_ids\": []}\n{\"item_id\": \"feed:https://ruckauthority.com/gear/goruck-rucker-vs-gr1\", \"version_id\": \"6a7bdc8341b414f9b53738017f3cd857f57d82067bb2658a7b431c509920499c\", \"decision\": \"reject\", \"reason\": \"Under Relevance, this is a comparison of two GORUCK packs that is mainly a buying guide and sales-oriented copy, with a promotional 'Where to buy' section and shop links. Under Commercial incentives, the source has affiliate commissions and GORUCK-supplied review units, and under Unsupported claims, many assertions such as 'the GR1 wins for most people' and 'the Rucker is better for training' are not supported by independent testing. Under Making the decision, the piece is a promotional post with no substantive new test data, so it is rejected.\", \"piece_ids\": []}\n{\"item_id\": \"feed:https://ruckauthority.com/gear/hyperwear-hyper-vest-pro\", \"version_id\": \"2f1600e0b4810c0d338f9df15eaf58c9fd6d3c09ea05f2a25ca878015f17c2e9\", \"decision\": \"defer\", \"reason\": \"Under Relevance, this is a weighted vest review and is in scope, but the reviewer states they have not personally tested the vest and relies on owner reviews from retailers and the manufacturer's own product page. Under Credibility, owner reports are unverified, and under Making the decision, the evidence is too thin to rely on yet, since the durability and warranty claims are not confirmed by independent testing. The piece also has a sales-oriented tone and affiliate-style ranking, so it is deferred until firsthand testing is available.\"}","ttft_ms":13762,"type":"result","duration_ms":13795,"uuid":"51c3e502-1e31-4a59-9c36-4e976498a18c","ttft_stream_ms":1193,"time_to_request_ms":85,"first_content_frame_ms":1193,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
